<!--
  Whole-body-controller stage plugins (issue #6, M2.1; reworked by issue #13, M3.2).

  base_class_type: StagePlugin<WBCInterface>
    (mit_controller/stage_plugin.hpp + mit_controller/wbc_interface.hpp
     + mit_controller/joint_commands.hpp)

  Both stock WBCs declare that one base. Until M3.2 they could not: WBCInterface was
  a class template keyed on the command struct (gap G8), so wbc_arc_opt registered
  under the JointTorqueVelocityPositionCommands instantiation and inverse_dynamics
  under the CartesianCommands one, and picking between them meant rebuilding the
  host for the matching instantiation. #13 de-templated the interface — the command
  family is now reported at runtime by WBCCommandMode SupportedCommandMode() — so
  the two collapse into one base and `wbc.type` selects either without a rebuild.
  This file was the only stage XML the collapse touched, as
  doc/modularity/plugin_discovery.md predicted.

  Stock wrappers (M2.3, issue #8): wbc_arc_opt and inverse_dynamics, in
  src/plugins/wbc_plugins.cpp, both built into libwbc_plugins — which has always
  been built robot-agnostically, so both classes are present in every build.

  The '<' in base_class_type is XML-escaped as &lt;/&gt; (stage_loading.md §5).
  The `name` (type: key) vocabulary is owned by M2.5 (#10); this file is
  naming-agnostic per doc/modularity/plugin_lifecycle.md.
-->
<class_libraries>
  <library path="libwbc_plugins">
    <class name="wbc_arc_opt"
           type="stock_plugins::WbcArcOptPlugin"
           base_class_type="StagePlugin&lt;WBCInterface&gt;">
      <description>ARC-OPT task-space inverse dynamics WBC producing joint torque/velocity/position
        commands (WBCArcOPT). Reports WBCCommandMode::kJoint, so it needs leg_control_mode 0 or 1;
        the stock Go2 path.</description>
    </class>
    <class name="inverse_dynamics"
           type="stock_plugins::InverseDynamicsPlugin"
           base_class_type="StagePlugin&lt;WBCInterface&gt;">
      <description>Inverse-dynamics WBC producing Cartesian foot commands (InverseDynamics).
        Reports WBCCommandMode::kCartesian, so it needs leg_control_mode 2 or 3; the ULab/ikin
        path.</description>
    </class>
  </library>
</class_libraries>
